<title>LEBANON: Short-term T-bill yields fall in Beirut.</title>
<headline>Short-term T-bill yields fall in Beirut.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields on short-term Lebanese treasury bills for the May 29 issue fell while long-term t-bill yields held steady, the Bank of Lebanon said on Monday.</p>
<p>The bank issued the following rate details (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				 percent)		    (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	   13.17 (13.21)		13.62 (13.66)</p>
<p>    Six months	     13.41 (13.44)		14.37 (14.41)</p>
</text>
